            <ArticleTitle>Intraoperative Nerve Monitoring During Nerve Decompression Surgery in the Lower Extremity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>255-66</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cpm.2015.12.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0891-8422(15)00126-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the benefits of intraoperative neurophysiologic monitoring (IONM) and proposes methods for integration into nerve decompression procedures. Standard procedures for intraoperative nerve monitoring (IONM) are illustrated as they would apply to the 3 nerve tunnels that have significant motor components within the lower extremity.</AbstractText>
